  "details": "Alright so this is a feature I wished for quite some time.\nI am very thankful they working on it but its not quite there yet.\nMajor issues I noticed:\n- The ChatBoxes of un-added people are by default disabled and there is no way for people to know how to enable them or that they have to enable anything in the first place, and VRChat player are not smart enough to just figure that out.\nThis leads to the chatbox being useless towards majority of players from the get go.\n- Height of the Chatbox, we use different sized avatars and generally it just be smarter to have one slider that controls the height of the Chatbox.\n- Chatboxes are invisible in the mirror and hard to see for VR players in most scenarios.\n- I heard u guys want to add a sound to make people aware of someone typing, I am against that I believe even if its just a chill sound it will annoy people leading them to disable it so it will be useless anyways",
